org2mid -- Cave Story Organya (.org) -> Standard MIDI File (.mid)
==================================================================

Linux host-side converter for the doskutsu DOS port. NOT a DOS binary;
NOT linked against the engine. Standalone C99 + libc.

Why this exists
---------------
doskutsu's MidiScheduler (vendor/nxengine-evo/src/sound/MidiScheduler.{h,cpp})
parses Standard MIDI Files and dispatches events to a chip-side backend
(WaveBlaster / DreamBlaster S2 via DSP-mediated MIDI per SDL/0047, OPL3
FM, or a no-op stub). Cave Story's freeware music is in Pixel's custom
Organya format (.org), so a build-time converter is needed.

Prior art (scripts/build-cs-midi-orgmid.py) downloads + builds Robert
Hart's ORGMID v0.82 C source from rnhart.net, then hacks +12 semitones
onto every note to fix ORGMID's known octave-down quirk. org2mid
replaces that pipeline with a first-party converter we own (GPLv3,
no network fetch, correct octave at first emission, configurable
loop-replication count).

Design reference
----------------
docs/internal/WAVE-41-CONVERTER-DESIGN.md (gitignored under
docs/internal/). All conversion decisions (PPQ choice, GM mappings,
loop strategy, edge cases) are documented there with citations to
the engine's Organya parser at vendor/nxengine-evo/src/sound/Organya.cpp.

Build
-----
    make

Produces ./org2mid in the current directory. C99 + libc; tested with
gcc -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic.

Usage
-----
    ./org2mid [OPTIONS] <input.org> <output.mid>

Options:
    --loop-strategy=N   Number of loop-body repetitions appended after
                        the intro (default 4). Higher = longer gap
                        before the intro re-plays at SMF end-of-track
                        loop-from-start. Range 0..32.
    --no-pipi-swap      Disable the pipi-flag GM-program swap (use the
                        base melody GM table for every instrument
                        regardless of pipi).
    --force             Overwrite <output.mid> if it exists.
    -h, --help          Show help and exit.

Exit codes:
    0  success
    1  conversion failure (malformed input, I/O error, etc.)
    2  CLI argument error

Self-test
---------
    make selftest

Converts data/org/quiet.org -> /tmp/quiet.mid and validates the MThd
header. Does NOT validate audible correctness -- that requires real
hardware (DreamBlaster S2 + WaveBlaster header on the operator's g2k)
and is gated by wave-41 task #4's listening session.

Output format
-------------
Standard MIDI File, Format 1, PPQ = 48, 10 MTrks:
    Track 0: metadata (tempo, time-sig, loopStart/loopEnd markers, EOT)
    Tracks 1..8: Organya melody instruments 0..7 on MIDI channels 0..7
    Track 9: Organya drum instruments 8..15 merged on MIDI channel 9

GM program assignment (sec. 3.1 of the design doc, subject to revision
after task #4 listening verification):
    Org track 0 -> GM 80 (Lead 1 Square)        [or 84 Charang if pipi]
    Org track 1 -> GM 81 (Lead 2 Sawtooth)      [or 85 Lead 6 Voice]
    Org track 2 -> GM 56 (Trumpet)              [or 60 French Horn]
    Org track 3 -> GM 73 (Flute)                [or 75 Pan Flute]
    Org track 4 -> GM 88 (Pad 1 New Age)        [or 89 Pad 2 Warm]
    Org track 5 -> GM 25 (Steel Guitar)         [or 27 EGuitar Jazz]
    Org track 6 -> GM 33 (Electric Bass finger) [or 34 EBass picked]
    Org track 7 -> GM 5  (Electric Piano 2)     [or 4  Electric Piano 1]

Drum mapping (sec. 3.2):
    Org drum 0 (BASS)       -> GM 35
    Org drum 1 (SNARE)      -> GM 38
    Org drum 2 (HI-CLOSE)   -> GM 42
    Org drum 3 (HI-OPEN)    -> GM 46
    Org drum 4 (TOM)        -> GM 45
    Org drum 5 (PERCUSSION) -> GM 39
    Org drums 6 + 7 are SND_NULL across the entire Cave Story corpus.

Known limitations (v1)
----------------------
- Organya per-event waveform field (`event.wave`) is discarded; melody
  GM patches are per-track, not per-event. v2 may add per-event
  program-change.
- Organya `tuning` field is discarded (MidiScheduler skips pitch-bend
  events per MidiScheduler.h:93-96; tuning would need a scheduler
  patch first).
- Organya drum-channel pitch field is discarded; every event on a given
  drum slot emits the same GM percussion key.
- Loop semantics emit `intro + N body reps` inline; the v2 fix is a
  MidiScheduler patch that honors the loopStart/loopEnd meta-text
  markers this tool already emits at the original tick positions.

